      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Meryetamun\", \"choices\": [\"C2\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Mr.t-Mnw is 'Meret-Min', the words mr.t ('beloved') plus the god Min (Mnw). Record 1 ends in -amun, which renders Jmn (Amun), not Mnw. Amun has the consonants j-m-n, while Min is m-n plus weak w, and the TLA's own translation names Min. So record 1 renders a different god and C1 is a different name. C2 Mr.t-Jmn is 'Meret-Imen', the words mr.t ('beloved') plus the god Amun (Jmn). Record 1 reads as Meryet = mr.t: m, r and feminine t are all rendered, and the y is a conventional vowel glide for the 'beloved' word, adding no consonant the candidate lacks. Then amun = Jmn: j rendered as a, m, a vowel, n. Same words in the same order, so C2 is the same name.\"}"
     }
